{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gnarled-acardiac-bettong","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nFound while investigating bug `wrongful-chemic-squeaker` (168e-8b84-087b-410e). It is NOT the\ncause of that flake, but it is a real, proven defect in the same function.\n\n`src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py`, in `_publish_and_prune`:\n\n    create = _git(base_path, \"bundle\", \"create\", bundle_path, \"HEAD\", f\"refs/heads/{ref}\")\n\nThe literal `HEAD` is bundled unconditionally. The function already knows HEAD may not be the\nref it is publishing — just above, it consults `git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD` and\nskips the `git branch -f` update when `current_branch == ref`. But the bundle argument does not\ntake that distinction into account.\n\n## Impact\n\nWhen `current_branch != ref` — a detached HEAD, a tracker with a different branch checked out,\nor a bare/mirror tracker — `HEAD` names an unrelated commit, so the bundle silently carries the\nWRONG tip alongside the correct `refs/heads/<ref>`. With an unborn HEAD the command instead\ndies with `fatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD': unknown revision …`.\n\nThe `HEAD` argument is load-bearing and must not simply be dropped: a bundle containing only\n`refs/heads/<ref>` clones with `warning: remote HEAD refers to nonexistent ref, unable to\ncheckout` and no commits, which breaks `s3_doctor_harness.healed_tip`. The fix is to make the\nbundled HEAD explicit and correct, not to remove it.\n\n## Evidence\n\nEstablished experimentally on git 2.55 while ruling out hypotheses for 168e:\n\n- unborn HEAD, and HEAD symref pointing at a missing branch, both produce\n  `fatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD'` (NOT `bad object`);\n- a bundle built from `refs/heads/tickets` alone produces the `remote HEAD refers to\n  nonexistent ref` warning and an empty checkout on clone.\n\nThe existing integration tests never exercise this: `_base_tracker` does\n`git clone -q -b tickets <content> tracker`, a normal non-bare clone whose HEAD is a symref to\n`refs/heads/tickets`, so `current_branch == ref` always holds and the defective branch is never\ntaken.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_publish_and_prune` bundles a tip that is correct when `current_branch != ref`.\n- [ ] A bundle produced when the tracker has a different branch checked out contains the\n      published ref's tip and no unrelated commit.\n- [ ] A bundle produced from a tracker with a detached HEAD is correct.\n- [ ] A clone from the produced bundle still checks out the published ref (no `remote HEAD\n      refers to nonexistent ref` warning, and a non-empty checkout).\n- [ ] A regression test covers a tracker whose checked-out branch is not the published ref;\n      it fails before the fix.","id":"2030-2d8e-73e6-4bf9","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","s3_doctor"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"s3_doctor bundles literal HEAD, bundling the wrong tip when the tracker's checked-out branch is not the published ref"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786502325658528001,"uuid":"adb66b51-742f-4826-976f-cdb6a70aaa07"}